# 6. Component Rules

Components have one responsibility.

Good

```
CareerHero

ProjectCard

ProgressRing

MentorCard
```

Bad

```
CareerDashboardWithProjectsAndSettings
```

Small components compose larger ones.

---

# 7. Server vs Client Components

Default

Server Component

Only use Client Components when necessary.

Allowed reasons

- Local interaction
- Browser APIs
- Animation
- Forms
- Drag & Drop

Everything else should remain server-rendered.

---

# 8. Business Logic

Business logic NEVER belongs inside components.

Incorrect

```
CareerCard.tsx

↓

calculates readiness
```

Correct

```
CareerService

↓

calculates readiness

↓

CareerCard renders result
```

Components display.

Services think.

---

# 9. Service Layer

Every important business process belongs in a service.

Examples

CareerService

ProgressService

RoadmapService

RecommendationService

PortfolioService

ResumeService

InterviewService

NotificationService

AnalyticsService

AIContextService

Services should contain no UI code.

---

# 10. Custom Hooks

Hooks encapsulate reusable behavior.

Examples

useCareer()

useProgress()

useRoadmap()

useDashboard()

useMentor()

useNotifications()

Hooks should not duplicate business rules.

---

# 11. Naming Conventions

Folders

lowercase

```
career

dashboard

projects
```

Files

PascalCase for components

camelCase for utilities

Examples

CareerHero.tsx

ProjectCard.tsx

careerService.ts

calculateReadiness.ts

---

# 12. TypeScript Rules

No `any`.

Prefer explicit types.

Every public function must be typed.

Shared models belong inside

```
types/
```

Never redefine shared interfaces.

---

# 13. Configuration

Never hardcode configurable values.

Move to

```
config/
```

Examples

Career categories

Roadmap weights

Difficulty levels

AI providers

Feature flags

Theme options

---

# 14. Constants

Static values belong in

```
constants/
```

Examples

Career levels

Badge names

Route names

Quiz limits

Notification types

---

# 15. Environment Variables

Never expose secrets.

Public values

```
NEXT_PUBLIC_
```

Private values

Server only.

AI keys must never reach the browser.

---

# 16. Validation

Every input must be validated.

Frontend validation

↓

Server validation

↓

Database constraints

Never trust client input.

---

# 17. Error Handling

Every service returns predictable results.

Never expose stack traces.

Errors should contain

- message
- type
- retry possibility

